  "query_preview": "..\nWeak trade wind showers are making their way over the Marianas this\nafternoon. Moisture is expected to stay high enough for this pattern\nto continue for much of the week. A brief island induced \nthunderstorm was visible off the coast of Guam today, but winds are \nexpected to continue to keep any isolated thunderstorms off the coast\nagain tomorrow. Decreasing wind shear will likely prevent any \nthunderstorm development on Tuesday with island effect showers\nremaining a possibility with the lighter winds. The location of a\npocket of drier air moving into the region beginning Tuesday could\nlimit the development of these showers, so keeping chances as\nisolated for now.",
